  "summary": "ACLU commentary surveying how Flock's ALPR system is expanding beyond simple plate-reading: ICE access, abortion-related searches, integration with data brokers, video and AI-powered search, a private 'Business Network' for corporate hotlists, and predictive analytics. Calls for state and local privacy protections.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "many of the searches were carried out by local officers on behalf of ICE for immigration purposes",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "a police officer in Texas used the system to search nationwide for a woman who'd had a self-administered abortion",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock is effectively automating and scaling the end run around our checks and balances that law enforcement data broker purchases represent",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock is turning its plate readers into surveillance cameras",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "shift the company from providing tools for officials to use in investigating suspicion to generating suspicion",
